{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>So YHWH blessed the Sabbath day and hallowed it.</b> He says that the Sabbath day shall be blessed and holy, for by way of remembrance He commanded to bless it and to honor it, and by way of cessation He commanded that it be holy for us and that we do no work in it. And R. Eli'ezer said: 'For YHWH blessed this day and hallowed it' — for He designated it to receive therein an additional measure of wisdom beyond all the days. And the way of truth I have written (in Genesis 2:2) under the verse 'Thus the heavens and the earth were finished,' and from there you will gain insight and understand <b>that in six days YHWH made</b> — it should not be missing a bet; rather, 'for in six days YHWH made, and on the seventh day He ceased and was refreshed' (Exodus 31:17)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The attribution 'ור\"א' is resolved as R. Eli'ezer based on his identifiable position cited in b. Berakhot; the phrase 'תוספת חכמה' is rendered 'an additional measure of wisdom.' The closing remark about the missing bet refers to the form 'ששת' (with bet) versus 'שש' (without)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:11:36.121920931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}